ected components (blocks) of an undirected graph: a collection of blocks, each the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions of its edges in ascending order; blocks are ordered by their smallest edge position.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The blocks partition the edges that are not self-loops.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"BiconnectedComponents","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/biconnectedcomponents","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BiconnectedComponents"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/Trees":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Trees","abstract":[],"title":"Trees","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/trees","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/BlockCutTree":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BlockCutTree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The block–cut tree of an undirected graph (Harary’s block-cutpoint tree): a node per block and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per articulation point, and an edge joining each block to each articulation point it contains."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Blocks are numbered as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blocks"},{"type":"text","text":", articulation points by their place in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"articulationPoints"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order). It is a forest: one tree per connected component with an edge that is not a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop; isolated vertices are no node."}],"role":"symbol","title":"BlockCutTree","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":